# kprompt-dash rules

## Repo

OSS local cluster dashboard (ADR-0011): Go 1.23 serving an embedded web UI. Read-first, run-locally tool. See `AGENTS.md`.

## Locked constraints

- Read-first; any mutation follows plan -> approve like the CLI. No silent cluster writes.
- Default to a local bind address; widening exposure requires an explicit flag + warning.
- kubeconfig via `client-go`; treat all HTTP input as untrusted.
- Honesty: label experimental views; never fake cluster data.

## Style

- `gofmt`; packages under `internal/` (`api`, `kube`, `bind`); UI embedded from `web/`.
- Rebuild embedded assets when the UI changes; prefer table tests.

## Checks

```bash
go test ./...
go build ./cmd/kprompt-dash
```

## Commits

Only commit or open PRs when the user asks.
